netcccyun/dnsmgr — https://github.com/netcccyun/dnsmgr
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 消失的彩虹海

OpenFrp's DNS provider layer draws on dnsmgr's provider specifications, its
carrier-line (线路) mapping tables, and its declarative form-schema metadata.
No dnsmgr source code is copied verbatim; the Go implementation is written
from scratch against the same provider APIs.

Note: dnsmgr vendors a copy of skoerfgen/ACMECert under app/lib/acme/ with the
original copyright header removed. OpenFrp deliberately does not derive from
those files and uses go-acme/lego for ACME instead.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fatedier/frp — https://github.com/fatedier/frp
Apache License 2.0, Copyright (c) 2017 fatedier

OpenFrp implements its own wire protocol and does not copy frp source. Two frp
designs were studied and independently reimplemented: the SNI-sniffing approach
for TLS passthrough (aborting the handshake from a GetConfigForClient callback
and replaying peeked bytes), and the pre-established work-connection pool.

